 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Money talk",
     "texto": [
      "To pay: **en efectivo**, **con tarjeta** or **a plazos** (in instalments). A **ganga** is something very good and cheap.\n\nIn everyday speech there are many expressions about money:\n\n- **estar sin blanca**: to have no money\n- **costar un ojo de la cara**: to be very expensive\n- **estar tirado**: to be very cheap\n- **apretarse el cinturón**: to spend less\n- **tirar la casa por la ventana**: to spend a lot\n\nIf you **ahorras**, you save money; if you **gastas** a lot, you are **derrochador**; if you spend very little, you are **tacaño** or **agarrado**. These are informal expressions: they are not used in a formal job."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "«Estar sin» and fixed expressions",
     "texto": [
      "With **estar sin** + noun we say we do not have something: **estoy sin blanca**, **estoy sin dinero**, **estoy sin batería**.\n\nFixed expressions cannot be changed: you say **cuesta un ojo de la cara**, not «cuesta un ojo de la nariz». Only the verb changes: **cuesta**, **costó**, **costará**.\n\nTo talk about a person's character we use **ser**: mi hermano **es tacaño**; mi hermana **es derrochadora**. To compare: **más… que**: ahorro **más que** tú."
     ],
